  "question": {
    "text": "The de-Broglie's wavelength of an electron in the \\(4^{\\text {th }}\\) orbit is \\(\\qquad\\) \\(\\pi \\mathrm{a}_0 \\cdot\\left(\\mathrm{a}_0=\\right.\\) Bohr's radius \\()\\)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & 2 \\pi \\mathrm{r}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\mathrm{n} \\lambda_{\\mathrm{d}} \\\\ & 2 \\pi \\mathrm{a}_0 \\frac{\\mathrm{n}^2}{\\mathrm{Z}}=\\mathrm{n} \\lambda_{\\mathrm{d}} \\\\ & 2 \\pi \\mathrm{a}_0 \\frac{4^2}{1}=4 \\lambda_{\\mathrm{d}} \\\\ & \\lambda_{\\mathrm{d}}=8 \\pi \\mathrm{a}_0\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}